@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-md-8 text-center mb-5">
            <div class="ohrbob-logo justify-content-center mb-3" style="font-size: 3rem;">
                <span class="ohrbob-logo-icon"><img src="~/images/ohrbob-logo.svg" alt="ohrbob" style="height: 1em;" /></span>
                <span class="ohrbob-logo-text">
                    <span class="char-1">o</span><span class="char-2">h</span><span class="char-3">r</span><span class="char-4">b</span><span class="char-5">o</span><span class="char-6">b</span>
                </span>
            </div>
            <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold text-body">The Story Behind Ohrbob</h1>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-md-8">
            <p class="lead mb-4">
                Hi, I'm Kai. I created Ohrbob out of a very personal need: I wanted a way for my daughters to listen to podcasts that was safe, reliable, and completely trustworthy.
            </p>
            
            <p class="mb-4">
                In today's fast-paced digital world, most podcast platforms are built around keeping you glued to the screen, pushing endless recommendations, and harvesting your data. I didn't want that for my family. I needed a system where I could curate the content, organize it into easily accessible "stations", and let them just press play—knowing exactly what they were listening to.
            </p>
            
            <p class="mb-4">
                That simple idea grew into Ohrbob. It became a powerful tool to manage feeds, track listening progress across devices, and organize audio exactly the way we wanted.
            </p>
            
            <p class="mb-5">
                But beyond my own family, I built this to give something back. I firmly believe in the power of open-source software and the amazing community around it. Ohrbob is fully open-source and self-hostable because you shouldn't have to trade your privacy for a great listening experience. You have the right to own your data, run your own server, and enjoy your podcasts on your own terms.
            </p>

            <div class="text-center">
                <p class="text-muted fst-italic">Thank you for being part of this journey.</p>
                <div class="d-flex justify-content-center gap-3 mt-4">
                    <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index" class="btn btn-primary rounded-pill px-4">Start listening</a>
                    <a href="https://github.com/ohrbob-org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline-dark rounded-pill px-4"><i class="bi bi-github me-2"></i> GitHub</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
